{#
   THE TITLE CELL — what the row IS, plus the line that qualifies it (S134i).

   This is the column a reader scans, and it was written eleven different ways:
   a bare `{{ x.nom }}`, a link, a link plus an `<em>`, a `div.admin-cell-user`
   with a hand-built avatar, a `<strong>` and a `<small>`. Same job every time.

   Parameters:

     title     the row's name. Missing ⇒ the empty cell, never a blank `<td>`.
     href      makes the title a link. Omit and it is plain text — do NOT pass a
               `#`, which is a control that looks live and is not.
     subtitle  the quiet second line: an e-mail, a reference, a location
     media     a pre-rendered `_cell_media` include, when the row has a face
     reason    passed to `_cell_empty`

   ⚠️ The subtitle is `.is-meta` and stays quiet in both themes. It is metadata,
   not a second title; a page that needs two equally loud lines has two columns.
#}
<div class="admin-cell-user">
    {% if media|default('') %}{{ media|raw }}{% endif %}
    <div class="admin-cell-stack">
        {% if title|default('') %}
            <span class="is-strong">{% if href|default('') %}<a href="{{ href }}">{{ title }}</a>{% else %}{{ title }}{% endif %}</span>
        {% else %}
            <span class="is-strong">{% include 'site/_cell_empty.html.twig' with {reason: reason|default('cell.unnamed')} only %}</span>
        {% endif %}
        {% if subtitle|default('') %}<span class="is-meta">{{ subtitle }}</span>{% endif %}
    </div>
</div>
